- 1 × H–H = 432 kJ
- ½ × O=O = 0.5 × D(O=O)

**Bonds formed:**
- 2 × O–H = 2 × 460 = 920 kJ

Setting up the equation:

$$-241 = [432 + 0.5 \times D(\text{O=O})] - [2 \times 460]$$

$$-241 = 432 + 0.5 \times D(\text{O=O}) - 920$$

$$-241 = -488 + 0.5 \times D(\text{O=O})$$

$$0.5 \times D(\text{O=O}) = -241 + 488 = 247$$

