### Compound Identification

1. **`N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(N[C@H](CO)CC1=CC=CC=C1)=O`** — This is a **dipeptide** (amide bond). Amides are among the least reactive acyl derivatives because the nitrogen lone pair strongly donates into the carbonyl via resonance (making the carbonyl carbon less electrophilic), and the amine is a very poor leaving group (strong base).

2. **`O=C1C=CC(O1)=O`** — This is **maleic anhydride** (a cyclic anhydride). Anhydrides are highly reactive in nucleophilic acyl substitution because:
