   - Ring opening generates a carboxylate, a good leaving group

3. **`O=C([O-])C1=CC=CC=C1`** — This is the **benzoate anion** (carboxylate). This is the **least reactive** species because:
   - The formal negative charge on oxygen provides maximal resonance stabilization of the carbonyl
   - The carbonyl carbon is extremely electron-rich and a very poor electrophile
   - There is essentially no viable leaving group (expelling O²⁻ is prohibitively unfavorable)

